--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧠 Introduction

Interfaces are used in Java to achieve:

✔ Abstraction
✔ Multiple inheritance
✔ Loose coupling

Java also provides special interfaces like:

* Nested Interfaces
* Marker Interfaces
* Comparator Interface

👉 These are important for OOP and interview preparation.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 1. What is an Interface?

An interface is a blueprint that contains abstract methods.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 Syntax

```java id="i1"
interface Animal {
    void sound();
}
```

---

📌 Implementing Interface

```java id="i2"
class Dog implements Animal {

    public void sound() {
        System.out.println("Dog barks");
    }
}
```

---

▶️ Using Interface

```java id="i3"
Dog d = new Dog();
d.sound();
```

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🎯 Features of Interfaces

✔ Supports abstraction
✔ Allows multiple inheritance
✔ Methods are public & abstract by default
✔ Variables are public, static & final

---

📌 Multiple Inheritance Example

```java id="i4"
interface A {
    void show();
}

interface B {
    void display();
}

class Test implements A, B {

    public void show() {
        System.out.println("Show");
    }

    public void display() {
        System.out.println("Display");
    }
}
```

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧩 2. Nested Interface

An interface declared inside another interface or class.

---

📌 Example

```java id="n1"
class Outer {

    interface Inner {
        void message();
    }
}
```

---

▶️ Implementing Nested Interface

```java id="n2"
class Demo implements Outer.Inner {

    public void message() {
        System.out.println("Nested Interface");
    }
}
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🏷️ 3. Marker Interface

A marker interface contains no methods or fields.

👉 Used to provide special information to JVM/compiler.

---

📌 Example

```java id="m1"
interface Serializable {
}
```

---

🔍 Common Marker Interfaces

* `Serializable`
* `Cloneable`
* `Remote`

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

⚖️ 4. Comparator Interface

Used to define custom sorting logic.

Located in:

```java id="c1"
import java.util.Comparator;
```

---

📌 Example

```java id="c2"
import java.util.*;

class Student {
    int age;
    String name;

    Student(int age, String name) {
        this.age = age;
        this.name = name;
    }
}

class AgeComparator implements Comparator<Student> {

    public int compare(Student s1, Student s2) {
        return s1.age - s2.age;
    }
}
```

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

▶️ Sorting Example

```java id="c3"
Collections.sort(list, new AgeComparator());
```

---

🎯 Why Comparator?

✔ Custom sorting
✔ Flexible comparison logic
✔ Frequently used in collections

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📊 Comparable vs Comparator

| Feature       | Comparable   | Comparator     |
| ------------- | ------------ | -------------- |
| Package       | java.lang    | java.util      |
| Method        | compareTo()  | compare()      |
| Sorting Logic | Inside class | Separate class |

---

⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Forgetting `implements` keyword
❌ Not overriding interface methods
❌ Confusing Comparable with Comparator

